// successful delivery, including events recorded while the receiver was disabled. Each goes out
// signed and addressed as of now, with its original event id. A failed event already waiting on
// its retry schedule (for example after the receiver refused it) is not sent twice: its retry is
// moved to now (`retries_brought_forward`), so calling this again after fixing the receiver
