// CreateFull: Bulk-create users from an array, deduping by verified email, through the same path sign-up uses.
// Plaintext passwords are Argon2id-hashed; Argon2id, bcrypt, PBKDF2/scrypt (Django, passlib),
// Firebase scrypt (with password_hash_config.firebase), Better Auth scrypt and Node crypto.scrypt
// `scrypt$N$r$p$salt$key` hashes are imported verbatim (a Node string with an all-digit salt is
// also a valid Django one and must be named: password_hash_algorithm scrypt_node or scrypt_django;
// scrypt_node takes salt_encoding, default utf8 = the salt text as written). A hash that does not
// describe itself is imported by naming it: password_hash_algorithm (scrypt, pbkdf2, md5, sha1,
// sha256, sha512, their _salted forms, hmac_sha256, bcrypt, …) with password_hash_params (scrypt n
// or log_n / r / p / key_length; pbkdf2 digest / iterations / key_length; md5 and sha*
// salt_position prefix|suffix; encoding and salt_encoding hex|base64|base64url|utf8) and
// password_salt; the hash may be the bare digest or `<salt>$<hash>` / `<name>$<salt>$<hash>` (e.g.
// `scrypt$<salt>$<hash>` with the parameters given separately). Every imported hash is checked
// with a constant-time compare and upgraded to Argon2id on the first successful sign-in; a format
// that cannot be checked is rejected per row (unsupported_password_hash, the message names the
// field). Each row may also carry external_id, image_url (alias profile_image_url: an https URL;
// an invalid one fails the row with invalid_image_url), created_at, phone_number / phone_numbers
// and organization_memberships (org by id, external id or slug, plus a role);
// create_organizations:true creates a missing org. Per-row failures are recorded, never fatal.
// password_policy "until_email_verified" holds the password of a row without email_verified true
// until an email on the account is proven by any route; a correct password is refused until then
// with password_not_yet_usable (a wrong one gets the normal failure). Body: an array of users, or
// { users, upsert?, notify?, create_organizations?, password_policy?, password_hash_config? }. An
// import never notifies the imported users: with notify false (the default) no email, SMS or push
// is sent as a consequence of the import, whatever templates are configured; notify:true is
// reserved for future welcome messages and currently sends nothing.
// POST /v1/user_imports.
